/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
.*.swp
# Cargo.lock is committed: reticle ships a binary, so reproducible builds matter.

# Claude Code session/worktree state
.claude/

# `reticle fpga` writes <top>.json and <top>.lpf beside itself when no
# --output-dir is given, so a run in the repository root leaves them there.
# Anchored to the root: testdata/ has tracked .json and .lpf that are inputs.
/*.json
/*.lpf
# The same flow, and the Vivado oracle harness, also drop an elaborated
# netlist and a Vivado script and constraints beside those. Six of them were
# committed by a `git add -A`, one of them 1.26 MB of generated Verilog.
/*.v
/*.tcl
/*.xdc

# Bench scripts: kept across sessions, never committed. See tools/local/README.md
/tools/local/
